\ Two non-recursive words that both fail AOT codegen with NC.13 (abstract stack
\ underflow): each declares one input but drops twice. Unfiltered, the trace
\ names both words on every enabled axis. `--trace-aot-word=keep-me` scopes the
\ trace to keep-me, so its freeze / codegen / instr lines appear and skip-me's
\ are filtered out. The build itself still compiles (and rejects) both words;
\ only the trace output is scoped.
keep-me: ( x -- ) [ drop drop ] ;
skip-me: ( x -- ) [ drop drop ] ;
5 keep-me
6 skip-me
